      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early 20th‑century Jermyn hosted coal mines, cut‑glass works, silk factories, and even a bottling plant, reflecting a varied industrial base.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jermyn%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Situated on the Lackawanna River, Jermyn lies about 12 miles northeast of Scranton, offering scenic river views.",
